 repair: "Current whole Store96xH sizing remains justified by real allocation; safe reduction must preserve immutable prefix capture while switching replay. Two-pass lazy rewrite now avoids no-op/refused retention. Actual source fixture verifies one decision scan with zero rewrites for :none/:refused/:dry-run, and second ordered rewrite pass before instant/clear for :reclaim/:recorded. Actual reclaim whole retention remains; no immutable prefix capture or streaming replay claim"
}
^"catchup-spool-shape"{
 state: "Design freeze for Foundations producer; no installed grant or source implementation yet"
 source: "One ephemeral spool per admitted flight; spool records hold exact normalized article bytes and bounded record metadata for second sequential parse. Keep only current header/msgid<=250, line count, offsets and running32byte chain"
 continuation: "At record end, pause network receive and hash its known immutable spool range with pgs-dcb-begin/read-demand/step/result in64byte windows; then fold chain32+digest32+msgid and resume. At batch END compare complete chain before IHAVE; second spool pass emits IHAVE and dot-stuffed body windows. Never retain record index or complete body lines"
 authority: "New operator peer-flight allowance owns resident heap, spool disk, simultaneous flights, independent spool worker count, per-turn work. Launcher subtracts dedicated peer heap once before DEFAULT storage planning. No StoreA/T or output/syncer slack as substitute"
 custody: "Grant before dial/spool open. Hold socket+spool descriptor and actual worker/queue through receive/hash/replay; local replay socket adds simultaneous descriptor. Cancellation revokes publication but retains custody until physical worker completion, join, close observation and spool cleanup; peerACK/local235 does not settle"
 caps: "Spool quota counts headers/metadata as well as body, so zero-line malicious records consume admitted disk. Insufficient grant holds/refuses before next write, cursor unchanged. Wire quantum yields/resumes, no silent truncation. Source octets and physical heap are distinct dimensions"
}
